    "updated_at": "2024-10-09T20:29:17Z",
    "body": "Very good example. To put in other terms, it sounds like the \r\n\r\n...\\<q>\\<RLI>...\\</q>...\\<span>...\\</span>... \r\n\r\nis, in Unicode terms, acting like:\r\n\r\n...**\\<RLI>**\\<RLI>...**\\<PDI>**...**\\<LRI>**...**\\<PDI>**...\r\n\r\nwhich _effectively_ adds a termination to the end that matches the very first \\<RLI> (since that is the unmatched one).\r\n\r\n...**\\<RLI>**\\<RLI>...**\\<PDI>**...**\\<LRI>**...**\\<PDI>**..._\\<PDI>_\r\n\r\nWhereas Manish's proposal would pin within to the isolate it belongs to, thus\r\n\r\n...**\\<RLI>**\\<RLI>..._\\<PDI>_**\\<PDI>**...**\\<LRI>**...**\\<PDI>**...\r\n",
