    "updated_at": "2025-09-14T17:24:11Z",
    "body": "Oh I randomly stumbled upon this issue while investigating something else and want to mention that this is a larger problem for ruby elements (`<rb>` in particular). A while ago I opened a CSS issue for it here: https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12327.\n\nThis is a bit more of a problem in this case because it means ruby bases may get fragmented even though they are supposedly isolated, which means that it now becomes non-obvious where exactly annotations should be placed. In my implementation I used the solution discussed here as \"isolate\" (processing these runs separately) since that makes things simpler for me and statically eliminates the issue (as opposed to having to trust the string-based isolation algorithm).\n\nSo solving this is also necessary for correct ruby handling, otherwise you're bound to get weird (and non-portable!) results like those in that issue.",
